description:
###### **Requirements:**

* Diploma/Specialist Diploma in relevant field
* At least 1-2 year working experience as ECO in Environmental & Occupational Health Safety
* Must be registered with National Environment Agency as Environmental Control Officer

###### **Responsibilities:**

* Advise/Report to the occupier of the workplace together with recommendations on remedial measures to be taken to prevent recurrence;
* Prepare and submit a Site Environmental Control Programme to the occupier of the workplace once every fortnight;
* Inspect the workplace to ensure all facilities and equipment relevant to the maintenance of environmental health are in proper working condition and do not pose any environment health hazard;
* Point out and discuss environmental health irregularities such as mosquito and fly breeding, rodent infestation, noise/dust/smoke/water pollution, poor housekeeping, earth littering, poor refuse management, poor maintenance of sanitary facilities;
* Assist the authorities to investigate outbreaks of infectious, vector-borne or food-borne diseases on the workplace and
* Organise campaigns, training courses and other activities to develop and sustain the interest of workers in maintaining good environmental health standards
* Any other jobs as assigned.
